    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6216025.careers?ShowJob=621275786": {
      "title": "Coordinator Annual Giving, Communications, Alumni Relations",
      "description": "6216025:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Coordinator Annual Giving, Communications, Alumni Relations Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 1 BREVARD COLLEGE DR,\n    \n                      Brevard, NC, 28712-4283,\n                      United States Job Category Staff Employee Type FT Non-Exempt Required Degree 4 Year Degree Travel 25% Manage Others No Minimum Experience 1 Year Contact information Name Ondrea Dory Phone 8286410360 Email doryoj@brevard.edu Description The Coordinator of Annual Giving, Communications and Alumni Relations strengthens connections between Brevard College and its alumni, donors, parents, friends, and community partners. The position coordinates annual giving, advancement communications, alumni engagement, and key advancement events. Working with Alumni Affairs and Development colleagues and campus partners, the Coordinator helps grow philanthropic participation, deepen alumni engagement, and create consistent, mission-focused communications and experiences. Key Responsibilities Annual Giving • Coordinate the College’s annual giving program for alumni, parents, friends, faculty, staff, and other constituents. • Implement strategies to increase donor acquisition, retention, participation, and giving. • Lead planning and execution of I � BC Day, including messaging, donor challenges, campus participation, and athletics fundraising. • Support leadership annual giving and help identify donors for major gift qualification. • Make annual and leadership gift solicitations as appropriate and document activity in the CRM. Advancement Communications • Coordinate advancement communications that support fundraising, alumni engagement, and donor stewardship. • Produce the monthly alumni and donor e-newsletter and quarterly advancement publications. • Develop and coordinate content for email, social media, appeals, events, and other digital channels. • Partner with Marketing and Communications to ensure consistent College branding and messaging. • Gather stories, photos, testimonials, and impact content from faculty, staff, students, alumni, and Athletics. • Maintain an annual advancement communications calendar. Alumni Relations & Engagement • Serve as a primary staff contact for the Alumni Board and support alumni engagement activities. • Recruit and engage alumni volunteers for events, mentoring, networking, and fundraising initiatives. • Partner with campus colleagues to connect alumni with students and strengthen lifelong engagement with the College. Events & Campus Engagement • Coordinate alumni and donor events, including I � BC Day, Homecoming, Scholarship Luncheon, Celebration of Philanthropy, and Fine Arts Gala. • Manage event communications, invitations, online registration, guest lists, logistics, vendors, and follow- up. • Work with campus partners and volunteers to deliver high-quality events that support cultivation, engagement, and stewardship. Collaboration & Institutional Support • Support annual, major, planned, and campaign fundraising priorities in collaboration with advancement colleagues. • Partner with Athletics, Marketing and Communications, Admissions, Student Life, Academic Affairs, and other campus departments. • Represent Brevard College at alumni, donor, community, athletics, and campus events. • Support special initiatives and perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required • Bachelor’s degree. • Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and project-management skills. • Ability to manage multiple priorities and build effective relationships with alumni, donors, volunteers, students, faculty, and staff. • Strong attention to detail and commitment to professional, accurate communications. • Ability to attend occasional evening and weekend events and travel for alumni and donor engagement. • Commitment to the mission and values of Brevard College. Preferred • Experience in fundraising, alumni relations, communications, marketing, events, higher education, or a related field. • Experience with digital, email, social media, or print communications and event coordination. • Familiarity with donor or constituent relationship management systems. • Experience with annual giving, donor solicitation, or stewardship."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6216025.careers?ShowJob=587673836": {
      "title": "Dishwasher",
      "description": "6216025:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Dishwasher Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 1 BREVARD COLLEGE DR,\n    \n                      Brevard, NC, 28712-4283,\n                      United States Job Category Staff Employee Type FT Non-Exempt Required Degree High school Manage Others No Minimum Experience 1 Year Contact information Name Ondrea Dory Phone 828-641-0360 Email hr@brevard.edu Description Brevard College Dining services provides campus-wide food services to students, faculty, and staff on the Brevard College campus and catering events on and off campus. The college serves 600+ residential students with the meal program. The department employs approximately 35 full/part-time and student employees.  Must be able to work holidays/weekends/evenings. Duties/Responsibilities: · Washes all wares including pots, plans, flatware, and glasses, by hand or using dishwashers. · Correctly places and stores clean equipment, dishes, and utensils in assigned storage areas. · Stocks serving stations, cupboards, refrigerators, and other assigned areas with necessary dishes and utensils. · Cleans trash receptacles with water or steam. · Moves dishwashing supplies and equipment from storage to work area by hand or using hand trucks. · May assist in cleaning and preparing various foods for cooking and/or serving, as directed. · Ensures work areas remain safe, clean, and orderly, adhering to all company, local, and state guidelines regarding health, safety, and sanitation. · Performs other related duties as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities: · Ability to understand and follow directions. · Ability to understand and meet restaurant standards for health, safety, and excellence. · Ability to remain alert and focused in an environment that is noisy and fast-paced. · Ability to work effectively with kitchen staff. · Detail-oriented and thorough. · ServSafe certified or ability to obtain within first 60 days of employment Education and Experience: · Restaurant experience preferred. Physical Requirements: · Prolonged periods walking or standing. · Must be able to lift, carry, and place up to 60 pounds at a time. · Must be able to work days, nights, weekends, and/or holidays as needed. · Must be able to bend, stoop, and wipe frequently. · Must frequently immerse hands in water. · Must be able to work in a hot and damp environment."
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6216025.careers?ShowJob=587700548": {
      "title": "Lead Cook",
      "description": "6216025:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Lead Cook Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 1 BREVARD COLLEGE DR,\n    \n                      Brevard, NC, 28712-4283,\n                      United States Job Category Staff Employee Type FT Non-Exempt Required Degree High school Manage Others No Minimum Experience 2 Years Contact information Name Ondrea Dory Phone 828-641-0360 Email hr@brevard.edu Description Fuel the minds of tomorrow! Brevard College is seeking a passionate and reliable Cook to join our dynamic Dining Services department . Whether you are grilling up student favorites for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, or showcasing your culinary creativity at special catered events, you will play a vital role in our campus community . We are looking for team players who thrive in a fast-paced environment and bring a positive, growth-oriented attitude to the kitchen . If you have a culinary degree or up to two years of experience and love creating great food, we want to hear from you ! Enjoy a role where no two days are the same, with flexible scheduling available . What you bring to the table: A passion for great food and a high standard for your workspace . The ability to stay organized and solve problems under pressure . A flexible schedule with availability for days, nights, weekends, and holidays . ServSafe certification (or a willingness to get it within your first 60 days) . Apply today to bring your flavor to Brevard College!"
    },
    "https://secure7.saashr.com/ta/6216025.careers?ShowJob=604447259": {
      "title": "Sous Chef",
      "description": "6216025:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Sous Chef Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 1 BREVARD COLLEGE DR,\n    \n                      Brevard, NC, 28712-4283,\n                      United States Job Category Staff Relocation Expense Covered No Employee Type FT Non-Exempt Required Degree 2 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 1 Year Contact information Name Ondrea Dory Phone 8286410360 Email doryoj@brevard.edu Description The Sous Chef supports daily kitchen operations by assisting in leadership, execution and quality control across all areas.  This role helps oversee food preparation, presentation, and service while ensuring consistency, cleanliness, and adherence to food safety standards.  The Sous Chef mentors and trains kitchen staff, assists with inventory and cost control, and collaborates with the Executive Chef to maintain efficient operations for our students and employees."
    },
    "https://brevard.edu/career%20advantage/": {
      "title": "Brevard College Career Advantage",
      "description": "Brevard College Career Advantage | Brevard College Skip to content Menu Brevard Career Advantage Your future is our passion. Your success is our purpose. The Brevard Career Advantage is a four-year individualized and adaptive career roadmap that leads each student to their desired career and post-college life. Brevard Career Advantage An Individualized, Adaptable Road Map for Every Student This program originated in an academic department. The success was overwhelming.  For those students engaged in this program over the past decade, almost 100% left Brevard College employed in their field of choice, or attending a graduate school of their choosing. Of those students who chose to go on to graduate studies, most attended with full-ride scholarships or graduate fellowships. That proven success has led to taking the program campus-wide and naming it Brevard Career Advantage. What makes Brevard Career Advantage so successful? The faculty at Brevard College are passionate about helping each student discover themselves, their career and their purpose. Every semester of a student’s time at Brevard College is partially engaged with creating and adjusting this roadmap. It is embedded in our curriculum in every major. It is central to our relationships. It is part of our culture. How does Brevard College do this? We commit ourselves to it. We do this by prioritizing relationships, experiences, mentoring, and individualized care. The Brevard Career Advantage starts when students arrive on campus their first year. They begin working with a personal advisor and First-Year Experience instructor. This process continues every semester until graduation. This effectively ensures that students are as well-positioned as possible for a career and life of success, meaning, achievement, and happiness. Results This program gets results. \"The unending support from my faculty for letter writing, phone calls about jobs, references, and resume editing is the only reason that I received the positions I'm in now.\" - Alex, MFA, Theatre Performance & Pedagogy 99% of Students Engaged in this program have been employed in their field of choice. Active Engagement Most colleges offer career services and career checklists. These approaches are passive. This program is different. It is an active commitment to an individualized, adaptive career road map for each and every student. How It Works Building Your Personalized Career Roadmap The Brevard Career Advantage means we’re here to support you every step of the way as you build a future you’re passionate about. Here’s a look at what you can expect in each year of your Brevard College journey: Year 1: Discover & Connect Your first year is all about getting connected—both to campus life and to the direction you want to take in your career. You’ll work one-on-one with your advisor to identify your strengths, explore different educational pathways, and find ways to get involved with the community. This is the time to discover your passions and start building a foundation for success. Personalized advising to discuss career interests and strengths Access to campus and community resources Support in discovering purpose and potential career pathways Year 2: Define Your Direction As you move into your second year, we’ll guide you in shaping a clearer vision of your future. Together, we’ll continue to design a personalized plan of courses and experiences that align with your goals and give you the expertise to stand out in your field. Tailored course planning with advisors to build relevant knowledge Opportunities to gain field-specific experience Creation of a personalized portfolio to highlight expertise and skills Year 3: Practice & Engage In your third year, it’s time to apply what you’ve learned and see it in action. You’ll engage with mentors, take on real-world challenges, and work with potential employers—on campus and beyond. This year is all about putting your skills to the test and developing the confidence to pursue your ambitions after graduation. Real-world experiences through internships and co-op placements Access to mentors and industry professionals Skill-building and practical applications of academic knowledge Year 4: Launch with Confidence Your final year at Brevard is all about preparation for what’s next. You’ll work closely with faculty and advisors to fine-tune your resume, craft professional communications, and prepare for interviews. We’ll help you make meaningful connections with potential employers and provide support as you organize applications, refine your presentations, and get ready for what lies ahead. Intensive support for job applications and graduate school admissions Networking events to connect with industry leaders and alumni Opportunities to engage with potential employers and mentors \"Dr. Brown in the History program helped me get an internship with the Great Smoky Mountains Association. That internship not only helped me learn more about the Parks Service, it solidified my decision to work there. It's my dream job!\" -Reagan, Brevard College Student \"We recognize that College means something different for each individual. We embrace individuality and seek to encourage each student to find a path that will help them succeed.\" -President Brad Andrews \"My professor sat down with me, and helped me figure out what I want to do. Then, she worked with me on classes and internships to help me get there.\" -Ollie, Brevard College Student \"Dr. Brown in the History program helped me get an internship with the Great Smoky Mountains Association. That internship not only helped me learn more about the Parks Service, it solidified my decision to work there. It's my dream job!\" -Reagan, Brevard College Student \"We recognize that College means something different for each individual. We embrace individuality and seek to encourage each student to find a path that will help them succeed.\" -President Brad Andrews 1 2 3 Faculty Who Care Our College-Wide Commitment to Your Career Success For those of us who work at Brevard College, this is not only our passion, we also view it as a central component of our job. All faculty and staff are committed to this program, to student success, and to positioning each and every student for the post-college life that most inspires them. Brevard Career Advantage is more than an app, more than an office, and more than a person. It is a campus-wide, one-on-one commitment to career development and success. Do You Have 15 Minutes? Apply for Admission You are more than a test score. The application is test-optional, FREE , and only takes 15 minutes to fill out. Apply for Free Today! Visit Brevard Register for an Open House! Tour campus, chat with current students, and speak with a financial aid advocate. Schedule Your Visit! (opens in new tab) Committed to Affordability Full-Tuition Scholarships Compete for the Full-Tuition, earn other scholarships, and get your FAFSA questions answered at the next Scholarship Competition! Register for the Scholarship Competition! The land of Waterfalls Live and Learn You'll find a caring community surrounded by an incredible natural environment. There's no better place to study the sciences. Life on Campus One Brevard College Dr. (opens in new tab) Brevard, NC 28712 (opens in new tab) 828.641.0641 (opens in new tab) admissions@brevard.edu (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) Brevard College is consistently recognized as one of the best liberal arts colleges. The College's focus on experiential learning, small class sizes, and location in the mountains of Western North Carolina near Asheville make Brevard a top choice college for students around the world. Consumer Disclosure Terms of Use (opens in new tab) Title IX (opens in new tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new tab) Whistleblower Policy (opens in new tab) MyBrevard © 2026 Brevard College This institution is an equal opportunity provider. Want to learn more? Sign up to download our quick fact sheet & stay up to date with Brevard College! Footer Interest Capture First Name * Last Name * Email * Graduating Year * If you are human, leave this field blank. Request Δ Academics Majors Minors & Concentrations Undergraduate Research Conference Graduate Programs Brevard Career Advantage Honors Program Find Your Career Path Admissions & Aid Apply for Admission Apply for Scholarships & Aid Confirm My Offer of Admission (Direct Admission) Pay My Enrollment Fee Register for a Scholarship Competition Register for Student Orientation Advising and Registration (S.O.A.R!) Schedule My Campus Visit Tuition & Fees Forms Campus Life Campus Life Graduation Information Clubs & Student Involvement New Student Center Student Success Career Services Outdoor Adventures The Town of Brevard Athletics Campus Ministry Institute for Women in Leadership Residence Life & Dorms Alumni & Friends Make a Gift Annual Fund Homecoming! Planned Giving New Student Center Donor Recognition Alumni Association Refer a Student About Brevard Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Brevard at a Glance Brevard Career Advantage Remarkable Outcomes New Student Center News Events Campus Map The Porter Center for the Performing Arts The J.A. Jones Library & ELC Contact Us Directory Post a Job or Internship Career Opportunities at Brevard Apply Visit Direct Admission Scholarships Pay My Enrollment Fee Make a Gift Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard (opens in new tab) News Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard (opens in new tab) News"
    },
    "https://brevard.edu/careers/": {
      "title": "Career Search",
      "description": "Career Search - Brevard College Skip to content Menu Liberal Arts College Career Paths Where can Brevard College take you? Choosing Brevard College leads to a degree that can take you anywhere. Career Search Career Area Select a Career Area Business & Finance Creative & Performing Arts Criminal Justice & Law Education & Social Service Healthcare & Wellness IT & Software Development Math, Analytics & Statistics Scientific Research & Development Writing & Communications Not sure, but I know what I want to major in. Not sure, and I'm undecided. If you are human, leave this field blank. Go! Δ Arts Careers & Majors Art Music Music Education Theatre Explore Opportunities in the Arts → Business Careers & Majors Business & Organizational Leadership Mathematics Accounting C-suite Officers Entrepreneurs Marketing Directors Explore Opportunities in Business → Healthcare Careers & Majors Health Care Professions Biology Exercise Science Health Science Physical Education & Recreation Explore Opportunities in Healthcare → Humanities Careers & Majors Childhood Education Communication English History Philosophy & Religion Wilderness Leadership & Experiential Education Explore Opportunities in the Humanities → Law Careers & Majors Criminal Justice History Psychology Lawyer Police officer Forensic Investigator Explore Opportunities in Law → Sciences Careers & Majors Biology Chemistry Environmental Studies Exercise Science Health Science Mathematics Psychology Physics Explore Opportunities in the Sciences → Tech Careers & Majors Computer Science Business & Organizational Leadership Information Technologist Data Analysts Computer Engineer Game Designer Explore Opportunities in Technology → Undecided Careers & Majors Integrated Studies Undecided Undeclared Explore Opportunities for Undecided Students → Apply for Admission to Brevard College Applying is the first step to deciding if a school is the right fit for you. Because financial aid status is so important for many students, our admissions application also doubles as an application for our Half-Tuition Scholarship! Apply for Admission Get all your big questions answered. Major and minor pathways. Career skills. Financial Aid. Campus life. Get the answers you need. We're Here to Help! If you have questions please contact the Admissions Office at 828.641.0461 or email admissions@brevard.edu (opens in new tab) . We are happy to answer any questions or help in any way! Sorry, we couldn't find any faculty for this department. Brevard is affordable Full-Tuition Scholarship Apply and compete for a Full-Tuition Scholarship at the Scholarship Competition on Saturday, December 12! Earn Scholarships Earn a degree & Start your career Remarkable Outcomes Brevard graduates excel in every field: CEOs of Fortune 500 companies, entrepreneurs, medical professionals, and C-suite executives, to name a few. Explore Graduate Profiles Explore Campus and the Land of Waterfalls Visit Brevard! Take a campus tour and learn more about Brevard. The next Visit Day is Saturday, October 24! (You can also choose a date that fits your schedule!) Visit Brevard! You are more than a test score. Apply for Admission You can choose to apply test-optional. The application is free and serves as your Merit Scholarship application! Apply for Admission! One Brevard College Dr. (opens in new tab) Brevard, NC 28712 (opens in new tab) 828.641.0641 (opens in new tab) admissions@brevard.edu (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) Brevard College is consistently recognized as one of the best liberal arts colleges. The College's focus on experiential learning, small class sizes, and location in the mountains of Western North Carolina near Asheville make Brevard a top choice college for students around the world. Consumer Disclosure Terms of Use (opens in new tab) Title IX (opens in new tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new tab) Whistleblower Policy (opens in new tab) MyBrevard © 2026 Brevard College This institution is an equal opportunity provider. Want to learn more? Sign up to download our quick fact sheet & stay up to date with Brevard College! Footer Interest Capture First Name * Last Name * Email * Graduating Year * If you are human, leave this field blank. Request Δ Academics Majors Minors & Concentrations Undergraduate Research Conference Graduate Programs Brevard Career Advantage Honors Program Find Your Career Path Admissions & Aid Apply for Admission Apply for Scholarships & Aid Confirm My Offer of Admission (Direct Admission) Pay My Enrollment Fee Register for a Scholarship Competition Register for Student Orientation Advising and Registration (S.O.A.R!) Schedule My Campus Visit Tuition & Fees Forms Campus Life Campus Life Graduation Information Clubs & Student Involvement New Student Center Student Success Career Services Outdoor Adventures The Town of Brevard Athletics Campus Ministry Institute for Women in Leadership Residence Life & Dorms Alumni & Friends Make a Gift Annual Fund Homecoming! Planned Giving New Student Center Donor Recognition Alumni Association Refer a Student About Brevard Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Brevard at a Glance Brevard Career Advantage Remarkable Outcomes New Student Center News Events Campus Map The Porter Center for the Performing Arts The J.A. Jones Library & ELC Contact Us Directory Post a Job or Internship Career Opportunities at Brevard Apply Visit Direct Admission Scholarships Pay My Enrollment Fee Make a Gift Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard (opens in new tab) News Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard (opens in new tab) News"
